---
import { legalDocuments } from "../../../site.config.mjs";
import { overLitConfig } from "../../config/site";

const appName = overLitConfig.name;
---

<h1>{appName} Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>
  <strong>Effective Date:</strong> {legalDocuments.overLitPrivacy.effectiveDate}<br />
  <strong>Version:</strong> {legalDocuments.overLitPrivacy.version}
</p>

<p>
  This Privacy Policy explains how {appName} handles information when you use the app, visit the
  small public app page under <code>/apps/OverLit/</code>, contact us, or interact with ads or
  campaigns related to {appName}.
</p>

<p>
  {appName} is provided by Aleksander Jałtuszyk (&quot;Developer&quot;, &quot;we&quot;, &quot;us&quot;,
  or &quot;our&quot;). Country: Poland. Contact: <code>{overLitConfig.supportEmail}</code>.
  Support page: <code>{overLitConfig.supportHref}</code>.
</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>

<ul>
  <li>{appName} is a mobile arcade game for short play sessions.</li>
  <li>The app does not require an account.</li>
  <li>Gameplay settings, preferences, and high scores may be stored locally on your device.</li>
  <li>
    We may show ads in the app, including ads served by third-party advertising networks or
    platform advertising services.
  </li>
  <li>
    We may advertise {appName} externally on services such as Apple Search Ads, Google, Meta,
    Instagram, TikTok, or similar platforms.
  </li>
  <li>
    Advertising partners and platforms may process information under their own terms and privacy
    policies. Your device, platform, and consent settings may affect what they receive.
  </li>
  <li>We may receive information you choose to send by email or another support channel.</li>
</ul>

<h2>1. Information We Collect Or Process</h2>

<p>Depending on how you use {appName}, we or our providers may process categories such as:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Local gameplay data, including scores, mode choices, settings, preferences, and progress</li>
  <li>Support messages, email address, and any information you choose to send us</li>
  <li>
    Website delivery and security information, such as IP address, browser type, request time, and
    similar hosting metadata when you visit this website
  </li>
  <li>
    Advertising information, such as ad impressions, clicks, approximate location, device type,
    app version, advertising or vendor identifiers where permitted, diagnostics, fraud-prevention
    signals, campaign source, and aggregated campaign reports
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

<p>We may use information to:</p>

<ul>
  <li>run the game and remember local settings or high scores</li>
  <li>provide support and respond to messages</li>
  <li>show, limit, personalize, measure, and improve ads where lawful</li>
  <li>understand whether external advertising campaigns are working</li>
  <li>detect fraud, prevent abuse, maintain security, and comply with law</li>
  <li>improve the app, website, and player experience</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. In-App Advertising</h2>

<p>
  {appName} may include ads. Ads may be served directly by us, by app stores or platform services,
  or by third-party advertising networks. Those providers may use information from your device or
  app session to deliver ads, cap ad frequency, measure performance, prevent fraud, and report
  aggregated campaign results.
</p>

<p>
  If the app uses tracking that requires Apple App Tracking Transparency permission or another
  legally required consent, the app should request that permission before using that type of
  tracking. If you decline tracking, advertising may still be shown, but it should be limited,
  contextual, or otherwise handled according to platform rules and applicable law.
</p>

<h2>4. External Advertising And Campaigns</h2>

<p>
  We may promote {appName} outside the app through paid or organic campaigns on third-party
  platforms such as Apple Search Ads, Google, Meta, Instagram, TikTok, or similar services. If you
  view, click, save, share, comment on, or otherwise interact with an ad for {appName}, that
  platform may process the interaction under its own privacy policy.
</p>

<p>
  We may use campaign links, referral information, UTM parameters, app store campaign reporting,
  ad dashboards, pixels, SDK events, conversion APIs, or similar measurement tools where lawful and
  with any required consent or platform disclosure.
</p>

<h2>5. Sharing</h2>

<p>We may share or make information available to:</p>

<ul>
  <li>service providers who help host the website, deliver support, or operate the app</li>
  <li>advertising networks, app stores, and campaign platforms used for ads or measurement</li>
  <li>law enforcement, regulators, or other parties when required by law or to protect rights</li>
</ul>

<p>
  We do not sell personal information in the ordinary sense of exchanging it for money. Some privacy
  laws define certain advertising or analytics disclosures as &quot;sale&quot;, &quot;sharing&quot;, or
  targeted advertising. Where those laws apply, you may have choices described by the relevant app,
  device, browser, or consent controls.
</p>

<h2>6. Your Choices</h2>

<ul>
  <li>You can use device settings to limit ad tracking, reset advertising identifiers, or manage app permissions.</li>
  <li>You can use iOS privacy prompts, including App Tracking Transparency where it applies.</li>
  <li>You can delete the app to remove locally stored app data from your device, subject to normal device backups.</li>
  <li>
    You can contact us at <code>{overLitConfig.supportEmail}</code> or through
    <code>{overLitConfig.supportHref}</code> with privacy questions or requests.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Children</h2>

<p>
  {appName} is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
  information from children under 13. If you believe a child has sent us personal information,
  contact us so we can review and delete it where appropriate.
</p>

<h2>8. International Processing</h2>

<p>
  We are based in Poland, and providers used for hosting, support, advertising, app stores, or
  measurement may process information in other countries. Those countries may have privacy laws
  different from where you live.
</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>

<p>
  We may update this policy as {appName} changes, including if advertising providers, measurement
  tools, or app features change. The effective date and version above show when this policy was
  last updated.
</p>
